1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 e5 5. Nb5 a6 6. Nd6+ Bxd6 7. Qxd6 Qf6 8. Qd1 Nge7 9. Nc3 O-O ({Too passive. Better is} 9... Qg6 {and 10...d5.}) 10. Be3 d6 11. Be2 Qg6 {Black has to get some counterplay - how else?} 12. Qd2 f5 ({Very risky but I couldn't stand being stifled. If now} 12... Qxg2 13. O-O-O {must win quite quickly.}) 13. Bf3 (13. exf5 {looks better to me - Black's pawns are so weak.}) 13... f4 14. Bb6 Be6 15. Qxd6 ({If} 15. O-O-O Nc8 16. Na4 {and Black seems to have a lot of pressure because of the bad position of the bishop on b6.} (16. Bc7 Qf7 {wins})) 15... Nc8 16. Qc5 Nxb6 17. Qxb6 Rad8 18. Ne2 (18. Qxb7 Bc4 19. b3 $1 {Speelman, 1997} (19. Nd5 Rxd5 20. exd5 Nd4 {wins}) (19. Rc1 Nd4 20. Ne2 Bxe2 21. Bxe2 Qxg2 {also winning})) 18... Bc4 19. c3 $2 (19. Qc5 Bxe2 20. Kxe2 Nd4+ 21. Kf1 Qe6 {winning probably.}) 19... Nd4 $1 20. Qc7 ({If} 20. Qxg6 Nc2+ 21. Kf1 Nxa1 $3 {wins nicely.}) 20... Nc2+ 21. Kf1 Rc8 22. Qxe5 Nxa1 23. b3 Rcd8 24. g4 Qh6 25. Kg2 Bxe2 26. Bxe2 f3+ $1 27. Bxf3 Rxf3 28. Kxf3 Qh3+ 29. Qg3 Rd3+ 30. Kf4 Rxg3 31. fxg3 Nc2 32. Rd1 Qh6+ 33. g5 Qe6 34. e5 g6 35. g4 Qb6 36. Rd3 Qf2+ 37. Rf3 Qxh2+ 38. Ke4 Qe2+ 39. Kf4 Ne1 {Source: bulletin; Source: Jon Speelman's Best Games by Jon Speelman (Batsford, 1997), p14} 0-1

