1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Be3 Bg7 7. f3 O-O 8. Qd2 Nc6 9. Bc4 Bd7 10. Bb3 ({An alternative here is} 10. O-O-O {, which avoids the ensuing continuation by Black.}) 10... Nxd4 11. Bxd4 b5 12. h4 a5 13. a4 ({If} 13. h5 e5 14. Be3 a4 15. Bd5 b4 $1 16. Ne2 Nxd5 17. exd5 Rc8 {with advantage to Black.}) 13... bxa4 14. Nxa4 e5 15. Be3 Be6 16. Nb6 Rb8 17. Nc4 $6 ({This is a new move. Alternatives are:} 17. Qxa5 Bxb3 18. cxb3 d5 19. Nxd5 Nxd5 20. Qxd5 Qxd5 21. exd5 Rxb3 22. Bc5 Rc8 23. Ba3 e4 24. O-O Bxb2 {drawing (Liberzon-Adorjan, 1971)}) ({or} 17. Nd5 Bxd5 18. exd5 Rb4 19. Ra4 Rxa4 20. Bxa4 e4 {with advantage to Black.}) 17... d5 $5 (17... Bxc4 {may be even better, e.g.} 18. Bxc4 Rxb2 19. Bb3 d5 $1 20. exd5 e4 (20... a4 21. Bxa4 Nxd5 22. Bc5 e4 23. O-O {is less clear}) 21. Bd4 Rxb3 22. cxb3 exf3 23. O-O fxg2 {with advantage to Black.}) 18. Nxa5 $6 (18. exd5 Bxd5 19. Nxa5 e4 {, with approximate equality, is better for White.}) 18... d4 19. Bg5 Bxb3 20. Nxb3 Qb6 (20... d3 {is stronger.}) 21. Qd3 Nh5 22. g4 Nf4 23. Bxf4 exf4 24. h5 Rfc8 25. hxg6 hxg6 26. Rh2 Rc6 27. Re2 Qd8 $1 28. O-O-O $2 ({Probably the losing move;} 28. Rh2 {is better when Black retains some advantage.}) 28... Qb6 $1 29. Kb1 Be5 30. Rh2 Qb4 ({Black could also play} 30... Qa7 {(intending 31...Ra8) and if} 31. Nxd4 $2 Ra6 32. c3 (32. Nb3 Ra1+ $1 33. Nxa1 Rxb2+ 34. Kc1 Rb1+ $1 35. Kd2 Rxd1+ 36. Kxd1 Qg1+ {and wins}) 32... Ra1+ 33. Kc2 Rxb2+ {and mate next move.}) 31. Qf1 $2 (31. Qd2 {is a better chance.}) 31... Qa4 32. Qh3 Ra8 {Threatening ...Qa2+ and 34...Qxb3.} 33. Rd3 Rca6 ({Not} 33... Qa2+ 34. Kc1 Rb8 35. Qh7+ Kf8 36. Qh8+ Bxh8 37. Rxh8+ Kg7 38. Rxb8 {with an unclear position. Now Black threatens ...Qa1+ and if 34 Kc1 Qb4 and wins.}) 34. Qh7+ Kf8 35. Qh6+ Bg7 36. Qh8+ {He might as well resign.} Bxh8 37. Rxh8+ Kg7 {(Informator gives this as game end but other contemporary sources continue)} 38. Rxa8 Rxa8 39. Rxd4 Qb5 40. Rd3 Rh8 {Notes by A.Adorjan, specially contributed. Sources: tournament bulletin, p33; Informator 16/410; The Chess Player (Nottingham), 5/720; BCM, September 1973, p355} 0-1

