1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Be3 Bg7 7. f3 O-O 8. Bc4 Nc6 9. Qd2 Bd7 10. h4 Qc7 11. Bb3 Na5 12. O-O-O Nc4 13. Bxc4 Qxc4 14. Bh6 b5 15. Bxg7 Kxg7 16. h5 b4 17. Nd5 Nxd5 18. exd5 Qxa2 19. Nb3 Bf5 20. hxg6 Bxg6 21. Qg5 Rfc8 22. Rd3 Kh8 23. Kd2 Rxc2+ 24. Kxc2 Rc8+ 25. Kd2 Qxb2+ 26. Ke3 Bxd3 27. Nd4 Bg6 28. Nc6 e6 29. Ne7 Rc3+ 30. Kf4 Qd2+ 31. Kg4 Qxg2+ {Source: unknown except that it appears on various databases, with 'Philippines 1973' given as place and date. Miles did not travel to the Philippines in 1973 though he did in 1974 when he won the World Junior Championship there. However, all his opponents there are accounted for and Azzopardi wasn't one of them. Much more likely that this Maltese player of similar age to Miles played him in one of the two 12-player all-play-alls which Miles took part in Malta in the summer of 1973. I'm making the assumption that it was the second and stronger of the two tournaments Miles played in Malta in 1973 though it could have been the first. JS} 0-1

