1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 {Played to avoid the Gruenfeld Defence.} e5 5. Nxe5 Nxe4 6. Nxe4 Bxe5 7. d4 Bg7 8. Bg5 f6 9. Be3 O-O 10. Nc3 $1 d6 11. g3 Bd7 12. Bg2 Qc8 13. Nd5 Nc6 14. O-O Rf7 15. Rc1 Ne7 16. Nxe7+ Rxe7 17. Qb3 $16 c6 18. Bf4 Bh3 ({An interesting echo of Petrosian-Botvinnik, 7th match game 1962, is} 18... f5 19. Bxd6 Re6 20. Bd5 $1 $18) 19. Bxd6 Bxg2 20. Kxg2 Re8 21. d5 Qd7 22. Bf4 Re4 23. Rfe1 Rae8 24. Rxe4 Rxe4 25. Rd1 cxd5 26. cxd5 Kh8 27. Rc1 h5 28. Rc7 Qf5 29. d6 Rd4 30. d7 Kh7 31. Rc8 Rxf4 32. gxf4 Qxd7 33. Rc1 b6 34. h3 f5 35. Rd1 Qc7 36. Qa4 a5 37. Rd7 Qc5 38. Qd1 Kh6 39. b3 Qb4 40. Qd2 Qe4+ 41. Kh2 Qc6 42. Rd6 Qc5 43. Kg2 Bh8 44. Qd5 Qb4 45. Qe6 Bf6 46. Rc6 $1 Qxf4 47. Qxf6 Qe4+ 48. Kh2 Qf4+ 49. Kg1 {Sources: bulletin; CHESS, February 1974, Vol.39/691-2, p153 (annotated by RDK); The Chess Player (Nottingham), 6/501; Dragon (Cambridge University CC bulletin), Lent (January) 1974} 1-0

