1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 a6 5. Nd2 d6 6. Bd3 Nf6 7. O-O Be7 8. Kh1 O-O 9. f4 Nbd7 10. Qe2 Nc5 11. N4b3 Nxd3 12. cxd3 a5 13. g4 e5 14. g5 Nd7 15. Nf3 a4 16. Nbd2 exf4 17. Rg1 Ne5 18. d4 Nxf3 19. Nxf3 d5 20. e5 Bf5 21. Bxf4 Be4 22. h4 Qd7 23. Kh2 Rac8 24. Ne1 Rc4 25. Rd1 Rfc8 26. Rg3 Bb4 27. Bd2 Rxd4 28. Bxb4 Rxb4 29. Rc3 Bg6 30. Rxd5 Rxh4+ 31. Kg1 Rh1+ 32. Kf2 Rh2+ 33. Kf1 Qf5+ 34. Qf3 Re8 35. Qxf5 Bxf5 36. Rb5 Be4 37. Nf3 Rh1+ 38. Kf2 Bc6 39. Rb4 g6 40. Nd4 Bd5 41. Rxa4 Rxe5 42. Rc8+ Kg7 43. Raa8 Rxg5 44. Rg8+ Kf6 45. Rad8 Rg2+ 46. Ke3 Rh3+ 47. Kf4 g5+ 48. Rxg5 Rh4+ {Source: Miles scoresheets (Geoff Lawton) - a possible anomaly here: BCM, August 1976, p341, probably reproducing the tournament press release (Leonard Barden? The wording of his Guardian column, 5 July 1976, is similar) states that "Miles beat N Benjamin, G van Dijk (NL), drew with T B Bennett, and beat N Short, J N Briggs and D E Rumens". However, the scoresheets show that Miles beat Wicker and Fuller and not N Benjamin and van Dijk. A mystery! The order in which Miles played his games is also problematic - I have gone with the order given in the Barden report, despite there probably being wrong opponents given there.} 0-1

