1. d4 {"I only play this move order against confirmed 1 d4 players. Then if they play 2 e4 I feel fairly happy with either 1...d5 or 2...b6!?" (Miles)} e6 2. c4 b6 3. d5 Qh4 $1 $146 4. e3 Nf6 5. a3 Bb7 6. Nf3 $6 (6. Nc3) 6... Qh5 7. dxe6 fxe6 $17 8. Be2 Qg6 9. Nh4 Qh6 10. Bf3 $6 (10. Nf3) 10... Nc6 11. g3 g5 $1 12. e4 (12. Ng2 g4 13. Bxg4 (13. Be2 Ne5 $19) 13... Nxg4 14. Qxg4 Ne5 $19) 12... Ne5 13. Bg2 Qg7 14. f4 (14. Nf3 Nxf3+ 15. Bxf3 g4 $19) (14. Bxg5 Qxg5 15. f4 Qg7 16. fxe5 Ng4 $19) 14... gxh4 15. fxe5 Ng4 $1 $19 16. Bf4 O-O-O 17. Nc3 Bc5 18. Qd2 Nxe5 19. b4 h3 $1 {Sources: BCM, June 1978, p246; Informator 25/115; The New Chess Player, 1/110} 0-1

